Q3b.en:
The inverse relation is obtained by reversing every ordered pair of \(R\):
\(R^{-1} = \{(5, 4), (4, 1), (6, 4), (6, 7), (7, 3)\}\).
The composition \(R^{-1} o R^{-1}\) contains \((a, c)\) whenever \((a, b) \in R^{-1}\) and \((b, c) \in R^{-1}\) for some \(b\):
- \((5, 4)\) and \((4, 1)\) give \((5, 1)\);
- \((6, 4)\) and \((4, 1)\) give \((6, 1)\);
- \((6, 7)\) and \((7, 3)\) give \((6, 3)\);
- \((4, 1)\) and \((7, 3)\) give nothing, since no pair of \(R^{-1}\) begins with 1 or 3.
Hence \(R^{-1} o R^{-1} = \{(5, 1), (6, 1), (6, 3)\}\).
